{
  "id": "micropublications",
  "content": {
    "description": [
      [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "In Research Methods for Graphic Design (third year), the course deliverables were double-sided 11″ × 17″ micropublications exploring a research question that could sustain multiple methods and matter to design practice."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "After Micropublication 1, I focused on the question: “How can technological advancements in augmented reality enhance the effectiveness of science communication?” It grew from my interest in how emerging tools can reshape how scientific information is shared, combining future-oriented interface design with science communication."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    ],
